body:
The undo/redo labels are passed as `t('designer.undo')` / `t('designer.redo')`, but the locale dictionaries define these keys under `appDesigner.undo` / `appDesigner.redo` (and there is no `designer` namespace). This will likely render the raw key strings in the UI. Use the existing `appDesigner.*` keys or add `designer.undo`/`designer.redo` translations consistently across locales.
```suggestion
            undoLabel={t('appDesigner.undo')}
            redoLabel={t('appDesigner.redo')}
```

The drag handle element is interactive (it receives `useSortable` listeners/attributes) but doesn’t provide an accessible name. Consider adding an `aria-label` (e.g., “Reorder {label}”) so screen reader users understand what the handle does.
```suggestion
                data-testid={`col-drag-handle-${colName}`}
                aria-label={`Reorder ${label}`}
```
